Room: permission prompts of Room pages go to the host.

Chrome draws a permission request as a Views bubble anchored on its location
bar (PermissionPromptBubbleBaseView, or the quiet chip). A Room page's
requests belong to the host's permission popover on the header's site button
(the Engine protocol's willAskForPermission, Phase 2.6a), which answers with
Accept, AcceptThisTime, Deny or Dismiss on the same PermissionRequestManager.

No existing hook: PermissionRequestManager creates its prompt through
PermissionsClient::CreatePrompt, which ChromePermissionsClient implements by
calling this Views factory; the manager's view factory is a test-only setter
(set_view_factory_for_testing) and the PermissionsClient is a process-wide
singleton Chrome owns. //room returns its prompt only for pages it wraps
whose delegate answers prompts; everything else keeps Chrome's bubble.

Phase 3.4a, 2026-10-05. //room: room/core/room_permissions.mm
(RoomPermissionPrompt).
